Hi again all hackers!

Thx a lot for you all out there who responds to all my spoiler questions.
I have finally recovered from the bag explosion as I just took the castle
with the WoW. I'M BACK IN BUISINESS!!!

Now as there might be some who hasnt played the 'good old Hack' I just
want to share my experiencies as I sometimes play Hack1.? om my amiga.
If there are some of you who has played an even older one than my version
perhaps you could fill in.

During the Hack days there were no katanas, polearms, etc etc. THE weapon
was the longsword (perhaps Excalibur) or in later stages the crysknife. 
I find it sad that this weapon (CK) has no big deal in NH3.x.x.

The only instrincts was fire/cold-resistance and poison resistance. 
Normally you ate just one monster corpse that had the instrinct
(killer bee, dragon or yeti) and that was it. No message, no nothing told
you about it. 

For armor there was the plate mail that we used. Also shield, pair of gloves,
helm and elven cloak. There were NO different ones though. No orc cloaks
etc etc, and no kind of boots.

Engraving worked beautiful, just E - "Elbereth" worked fine against every-
thing exept a dragons breath (or perhaps exploding spheres).

Polypiling didnt work as good as in later versions in a way. It only changed
the TOP object of the pile. That meant you had to lay down a row of objects
to polymorph. Still, wands that were polymorphed got recharged when you
zapped them so having a few wands you could go on for hours, just like
in early NH3.0 when the boxes that were polypiled gave you things.

Robbing shops was like stealing candy from kids. After the alarm went off
hundreds of WEAK cops came but almost every one that got killed produced
an item!! That meant that even the smallest shop was a source for hundereds
of items. The shopkeeper came after you of course, but only yelled -: Hey,
you forgot to pay!
Spellbooks came later than Hack. Tools were just the pick-axe, whistle
and the large box (= ice box). Hope I didnt forget some here.

There might be many more things that I have forgotten, (Maybe I have written
to much already for some) but I hope you got the hint.

During those dayes I made a (for NH3+) unbeatable record. I finished
the Wiz by only entering level 1, 2 and 35!!
That was possible by robbing a shop on level 2. Kill all the cops and
put all stuff in nice big piles. Get killed and hope for a bones.level.
Theese were almost a sure thing if there were many items and monsters
on the level.
Repeat two times.
Get the stuff. Quaff, read etc etc and finally teleport down to hell.
In Hack you ALWAYS found the Wiz's castle at the first attempt. Finishing
him off with a +5 crysknife was as easy as a snap with the fingers.
After leaving level one with the dog (or a shopkeeper I think) got a
line on the highscore list: Escaped the dungeon with amulet and a dog
(and a shopkeeper I think again).

Well, how good were those days? For you who has only played NH3+ or
perhaps even NH2+ it probably seemes like 'rogue' (No I dont
hate rogue. That is a VERY GOOD GAME TO.). But for us who played it
it was SUPER! I can still remember the days when we were 5 or 6 at
my work who started 17.00 sharp with the Hack session. The highscores
were creeping deeper and deeper down and every new level was an adventure.
The first guy who entered the mazes felt like a hero, not to speak about
him who finally found the 'trick' to teleport down to hell. I dont think
that I have ever had the same feelings again about Nethack, even if I find
that the D-team is doing a wonderful job out there. (Perhaps is the amnesia
scroll what I should read to get back to zero with this game).

Any way, I sometimes starts a Speliologist (sp?) to read:

-:Hello Janne! Welcome to Hack!

and it just feels fine!

                     Janne


